infographic hierarchy-tree-curved-line-rounded-rect-node
data
  root
    label Every TS name lives in value space, type space, or both
    children
      - label Value space only — const, let, function
        desc Exist at runtime, no type-space meaning. Survive to runtime; reach a type position only via typeof.
      - label Type space only — type, interface
        desc Erased before runtime, so no value exists. You cannot instanceof an interface; use them only in type positions.
      - label Both spaces — class, enum, namespace
        desc Registered in both tables and survive to runtime. A class is the constructor in value position, the instance type in type position.
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6 #f59e0b
